  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:65:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Praise waiteth for thee, O God, in Sion: and unto thee shall the vow be performed.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 65:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:65:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:65:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "O thou that hearest prayer, unto thee shall all flesh come.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 65:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:65:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:65:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Iniquities prevail against me: as for our transgressions, thou shalt purge them away.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 65:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:65:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:65:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Blessed is the man whom thou choosest, and causest to approach unto thee, that he may dwell in thy courts: we shall be satisfied with the goodness of thy house, even of thy holy temple.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 65:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:65:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:65:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "By terrible things in righteousness wilt thou answer us, O God of our salvation; who art the confidence of all the ends of the earth, and of them that are afar off upon the sea:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 65:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:65:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:65:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Which by his strength setteth fast the mountains; being girded with power:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 65:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:65:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:65:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Which stilleth the noise of the seas, the noise of their waves, and the tumult of the people.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 65:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:65:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:65:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "They also that dwell in the uttermost parts are afraid at thy tokens: thou makest the outgoings of the morning and evening to rejoice.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 65:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:65:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:65:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Thou visitest the earth, and waterest it: thou greatly enrichest it with the river of God, which is full of water: thou preparest them corn, when thou hast so provided for it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 65:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:65:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:65:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Thou waterest the ridges thereof abundantly: thou settlest the furrows thereof: thou makest it soft with showers: thou blessest the springing thereof.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 65:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:65:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:65:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Thou crownest the year with thy goodness; and thy paths drop fatness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 65:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:65:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:65:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "They drop upon the pastures of the wilderness: and the little hills rejoice on every side.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 65:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:65:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:65:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "The pastures are clothed with flocks; the valleys also are covered over with corn; they shout for joy, they also sing.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 65:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:65:13"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
